{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1307 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "9c8c76cb271aa40f5bf179f1eae461cbb7ca4a1e84c54b20515025dedf3c7059" :edb/db-before-t 1306 :edb/db-after-t 1307 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534619 50 #inst "2026-10-08T02:38:50.922Z" 13194139534619 true] [17592186064232 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299259 13194139534619 true] [17592186064232 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299273 13194139534619 true] [17592186064232 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299276 13194139534619 true] [17592186064233 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299252 13194139534619 true] [17592186064233 1020 #edb/ref 17592186299266 13194139534619 true] [17592186299252 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299253 13194139534619 true] [17592186299252 1089 "q-103771" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299252 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534619 true] [17592186299252 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/assets/68786f08e73998de597d0d9eea5be3031f322785c05835cf7eccfa7837f36d7b.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. It consists of two lines and the arc of a semi-circle of radius $3.$ Given $g(t)={\\int }_{-3}^{t}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ determine the value of $g(6).$" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299252 1113 #uuid "2db2de8c-b623-527a-a241-ca9def43988b" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299252 1145 "Evaluating $g(t)$ at $t=6,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\ng(6)={\\int }_{-3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral gives the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/assets/b553755a624031408b8374d06c8dc8dbf33c3ddc8d372332c945bad7e42ef068.png)\n\nNote that the graph above consists of $2$ parts:\n\n- $x\\in [-3,0],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a triangle. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{1}.$\n\n- $x\\in [0,6],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a semi-circle and a rectangle below it. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\ng(6)={\\int }_{-3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-3}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute these integrals:\n\n- To find the first integral where $x\\in [-3,0],$ we compute the area ${A}_{1}$ of the triangle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the second integral where $x\\in [0,6],$ we compute the area ${A}_{2}$ of the semi-circle and the rectangle below it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2}+bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}+6\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\pi +18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(3) & ={\\int }_{-3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=\\frac{9}{2}+(\\frac{9}{2}\\pi +18)=\\frac{45+9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299254 13194139534619 true] [17592186299253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299255 13194139534619 true] [17592186299253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299256 13194139534619 true] [17592186299253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299257 13194139534619 true] [17592186299253 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299258 13194139534619 true] [17592186299253 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534619 true] [17592186299253 1041 "selection" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299253 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299258 13194139534619 true] [17592186299253 1110 #uuid "b1e47631-c32b-5c32-9d8a-459bc3b07a5a" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299254 1034 "23+9\\pi " 13194139534619 true] [17592186299254 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299254 1111 #uuid "9818ae35-c8b3-5f88-ba2b-5d45142a8bf6" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299255 1034 "\\frac{36+9\\pi }{2}" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299255 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299255 1111 #uuid "73906657-1425-51ce-a538-2aa005fbfb8f" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299256 1034 "18+9\\pi " 13194139534619 true] [17592186299256 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299256 1111 #uuid "47f2bfd2-8877-5c8d-baeb-95219fbfd2f8" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299257 1034 "\\frac{45+18\\pi }{2}" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299257 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299257 1111 #uuid "83b79d39-0888-504f-8c23-2da1887a9f15" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299258 1034 "\\frac{45+9\\pi }{2}" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299258 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299258 1111 #uuid "87333285-38e3-5507-b35f-2d193c3ba5c2" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299259 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299260 13194139534619 true] [17592186299259 1089 "q-103776" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299259 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534619 true] [17592186299259 1100 "The bacteria culture in a lab increases at a rate of ${e}^{2t}$ per hour. If, after $2$ hours, there are $2\\,000$ bacteria in the population, approximately how many bacteria are in the population after $6$ hours?" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299259 1113 #uuid "8de63944-9034-5911-a181-23fee9b4f403" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299259 1145 "Let $s(t)={e}^{2t}$ be the rate at which the number of bacteria is changing and let $S(T)$ be the total number of bacteria and in the population after $T$ hours.\n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nS(T)=S(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{T}s(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S(T) & =S(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{T}s(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\,000+{\\int }_{2}^{T}{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}{|}_{2}^{T} \\\\  & =2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2T}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2T}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the number of bacteria in the culture after $T=6$ hours, we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\nS(6)=2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2\\cdot 6}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4}=2\\,000+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{12}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4}≈83\\,350.\n$$" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299261 13194139534619 true] [17592186299260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299262 13194139534619 true] [17592186299260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299263 13194139534619 true] [17592186299260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299264 13194139534619 true] [17592186299260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299265 13194139534619 true] [17592186299260 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534619 true] [17592186299260 1041 "selection" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299260 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299265 13194139534619 true] [17592186299260 1110 #uuid "8ddf580e-bb8e-58b9-8619-130ffdcec2ff" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299261 1034 "73\\,225" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299261 1111 #uuid "2c8a8d6e-233e-5b48-8976-c06358afb546" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299262 1034 "69\\,270" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299262 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299262 1111 #uuid "e39d5695-9efa-5e4a-ab6b-7ea5f9ffed29" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299263 1034 "89\\,850" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299263 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299263 1111 #uuid "6fdb847b-1d92-5ccb-ba6b-56b98999ccef" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299264 1034 "78\\,250" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299264 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299264 1111 #uuid "ceb86ed1-24f7-56df-a21e-7d7d67c11dde" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299265 1034 "83\\,350" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299265 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299265 1111 #uuid "3637a9d0-2e3a-5d25-a194-e01b7625e8e6" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299266 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299267 13194139534619 true] [17592186299266 1089 "q-156194" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299266 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534619 true] [17592186299266 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/assets/1a3b8289936cd2597ac1252e2b28987f245a7c4e88dcf3677e1ba3626460688b.png)\n\nThe graph of a function $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Given $g(t)={\\int }_{0}^{t}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x,$ determine the value of $g(3).$" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299266 1113 #uuid "42f9929a-0a88-505d-9ee3-e11f565821f9" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299266 1145 "Evaluating $g(t)$ at $t=3,$ we get the following definite integral:\n\n$$\ng(3)={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThis integral gives the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038411/assets/b5becb438f3bc8ab5445e116ddb64bf168013301838231bdc4d32d34283da5f1.png)\n\nNote that the graph above consists of $2$ parts:\n\n- $x\\in [0,1],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is a trapezoid. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{1}.$\n\n- $x\\in [1,3],$ for which the region between the curve and the $x$-axis is another trapezoid. This corresponds to the area ${A}_{2}.$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\ng(2)={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute these integrals:\n\n- To find the first integral where $x\\in [0,1],$ we compute the area ${A}_{1}$ of the trapezoid as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1\\cdot (2+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To find the second integral where $x\\in [1,3],$ we compute the area ${A}_{2}$ of the triapezoid as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot (2+3) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}=\\frac{5}{2}+5=\\frac{15}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299268 13194139534619 true] [17592186299267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299269 13194139534619 true] [17592186299267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299270 13194139534619 true] [17592186299267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299271 13194139534619 true] [17592186299267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299272 13194139534619 true] [17592186299267 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534619 true] [17592186299267 1041 "selection" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299267 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299271 13194139534619 true] [17592186299267 1110 #uuid "b1e91b78-4ebe-5e83-b2a4-73b4a74119bd" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299268 1034 "8" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299268 1111 #uuid "0c6b9d63-00c5-5523-af96-e5386eabdd37" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299269 1034 "7" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299269 1111 #uuid "212160bb-b2d8-55d2-9748-1cb73911f520" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299270 1034 "\\frac{11}{2}" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299270 1111 #uuid "d2bd244a-213a-55ab-9a18-cd8dada4f7ab" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299271 1034 "\\frac{15}{2}" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299271 1111 #uuid "4870f15d-97ab-552c-a447-e8dc2ef72fcc" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299272 1034 "5" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299272 1111 #uuid "b2ac04bc-2f57-5f8b-9435-10bae347d568" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299273 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299274 13194139534619 true] [17592186299273 1089 "q-316254" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299273 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534619 true] [17592186299273 1100 "In $2005$, a group of scientists started tracking the population of sea turtles in a coastal sanctuary. The initial population was $180,$ and the birth and death rates are given by $4+1.5t$ and $1+0.5t,$ respectively, where $t$ is the number of years since $2005.$  \n\nFind an expression for the population $P(t)$ of sea turtles in the sanctuary at any time $t>0.$\n\n$P(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299273 1113 #uuid "40532706-be5f-599b-966e-446d109da71f" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299273 1145 "Let $p(t)$ be the rate of change of the population. According to the given information,\n\n$$\np(t)={{4+1.5t}_{⏟}}_{\\text{population increase}}-{{(1+0.5t)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{population decrease}}=t+3.\n$$\n\nLet $P(T)$ represent the population of turtles $T$ years after $2005.$ By the accumulation of change formula, we have\n\n$$\nP(T)=P(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}p(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(T) & =P(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}p(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =180+{\\int }_{0}^{T}(t+3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =180+(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}+3t){|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =180+\\frac{1}{2}{T}^{2}+3T.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable  $t.$ We get \n\n$$\nP(t)=180+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}+3t.\n$$" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299275 13194139534619 true] [17592186299274 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534619 true] [17592186299274 1041 "field-1" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299274 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299275 13194139534619 true] [17592186299274 1110 #uuid "db546a25-11bf-5aa0-aec7-adaf7e1a4438" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299275 1034 "180+3t+0.5t^2" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534619 true] [17592186299275 1111 #uuid "30eaa84d-9078-5589-bfbc-a6316643e872" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299276 1017 #edb/ref 17592186299277 13194139534619 true] [17592186299276 1089 "q-49315" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299276 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534619 true] [17592186299276 1100 "A bicycle tire has a pressure of $6\\,\\text{psi}.$ It is being inflated, and the pressure is increasing at a rate of $4t\\,\\text{psi}$ per second, where $t$ is a time, in seconds, since the start of the inflation. The tire has a slow puncture that reduces pressure at a rate of $(t+2)\\,\\text{psi}$ per second. Identify an expression for $P(t),$ the total pressure in the tire at any time $t\\ge 0.$" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299276 1113 #uuid "b01cc438-929e-58bd-85f1-0598039ce8e6" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299276 1145 "Let $p(t)=4t-(t+2)=3t-2$ be the rate at which the pressure in the tire is changing. Note that we subtract $(t+2)$ to indicate the rate at which the pressure is decreasing.\n\nLet $P(T)$ be the pressure in the tire after $T$ seconds. Then, using our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nP(T)=P(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}p(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(T) & =P(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}p(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6+{\\int }_{0}^{T}(3t-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6+{(\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-2t)|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =6+\\frac{3}{2}{T}^{2}-2T \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{T}^{2}-2T+6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's rewrite our final answer in terms of the original variable $t.$ We have\n\n$$\nP(t)=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-2t+6.\n$$" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299278 13194139534619 true] [17592186299277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299279 13194139534619 true] [17592186299277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299280 13194139534619 true] [17592186299277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299281 13194139534619 true] [17592186299277 1000 #edb/ref 17592186299282 13194139534619 true] [17592186299277 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534619 true] [17592186299277 1041 "selection" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299277 1104 #edb/ref 17592186299278 13194139534619 true] [17592186299277 1110 #uuid "65c63586-7c82-5ed1-81b1-8e8127b1e4ae" 13194139534619 true] [17592186299278 1034 "P(t)=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{2}-2t+6" 13194139534619 true] [17592